     2	
     3	Status: resolved
     4	Blocked by: —
     5	
     6	## Files
     7	
     8	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/Models.swift` — `ExercisePreset`; `Exercise.presets`;
     9	  `ExerciseEntry.preset` + `snapshotPresetID`/`snapshotPresetName`;
    10	  `MachineInstance.defaultPresetID`; registered in `WorkoutTrackerStore.modelTypes`.
    11	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/ExercisePresets.swift` — naming and ordering rules (pure).
    12	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/RecordsMath.swift` — `presetID` on `RecordSetInput`, preset in every
    13	  `RecordGroupKey`.
    14	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/PreviousPerformance.swift` — layers, prefill and record summaries filter
    15	  by preset.
    16	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/WorkoutSession.swift` — snapshot capture, `usualPreset`, `choosePreset`.
    17	
    18	## Acceptance criteria
    19	
    20	- [x] Every new field is optional or defaulted, so the store already on the user's phone migrates
    21	      lightweightly. Sets logged before presets keep `nil` — honestly "no preset recorded".
    22	- [x] A preset is captured into the D23 snapshot at first completion and never rewritten; renaming
    23	      a preset afterwards does not retitle logged sets.
    24	- [x] Switching preset on a frozen entry splits it (D19), moving draft rows and leaving completed
    25	      sets behind — the same rule and the same shape as `chooseEquipment`.
    26	- [x] Records, previous performance and prefill never cross presets (D36).
    27	- [x] A machine's usual preset preselects a new entry, and a stale one degrades to none.
    28	- [x] Presets attached to a **seeded** exercise survive a catalog version bump (D24/D27).
    29	- [x] No UI import in `Domain/`.
    30	
    31	## Resolution (2026-08-12)
    32	
    33	`ExercisePresetTests` covers the lot, including the catalog-bump survival case that D27 taught us
    34	to check. The one design note worth keeping: `MachineInstance.defaultPresetID` is a scalar id
    35	resolved against the exercise being logged, not a relationship — a default pointing at another
    36	exercise's preset must degrade to "none chosen" rather than attach a variation from a different
    37	movement.
     1	# 03 — Choosing the preset while logging
     2	
     3	Status: resolved
     4	Blocked by: 02
     5	
     6	## Files
     7	
     8	- `WorkoutTracker/Features/ActiveWorkout/ExerciseEntryCard.swift` — the chip row.
     9	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/HistoryRendering.swift` — the preset in the snapshot equipment label.
    10	
    11	## Acceptance criteria
    12	
    13	- [x] Chips, not a menu: switched one-handed mid-workout, and seeing the alternatives is the point
    14	      — the user is choosing which record table the set belongs to.
    15	- [x] A "None" chip exists. The user did something the presets do not describe, and filing it under
    16	      a variation they did not perform would be the same lie as the wrong machine.
    17	- [x] The selection shows the live pick while drafting and the frozen snapshot once a set is
    18	      logged; switching after that splits the entry (the service owns the rule, not the view).
    19	- [x] History and the previous-performance sheet name the preset wherever they name the machine.
    20	- [x] Identifiers: `presetChip.<name>`, `presetChip.None`.
     1	# 04 — Export, docs, verification
     2	
     3	Status: resolved
     4	Blocked by: 03
